PowOS: CFS bandwidth control without changing struct cfs_rq / struct task_group (KMI-preserving)

OnePlus Open (GKI android13-5.15). CFS_BANDWIDTH normally adds fields to struct cfs_rq (embedded in
struct rq) and a struct cfs_bandwidth to struct task_group; the vendor scheduler modules (sched-walt,
oplus_bsp_sched_assist, oplus_bsp_frame_boost, ...) read both at fixed offsets. Here the per-cfs_rq
state moves to struct cfs_rq_bw - allocated behind each group cfs_rq (struct cfs_rq_ext), per-CPU for
the root cfs_rq in struct rq - and the group's cfs_bandwidth behind the task_group (struct
task_group_ext, root_cfs_bandwidth for the root group). Accessors: cfs_rq_bw(), tg_cfs_bandwidth().
Layouts stay stock; genksyms sees the stock definitions (__GENKSYMS__), so CRCs stay stock.

